<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`<<~ kukali trigger="on-score">>` declares a WAIT inside a causal island, until a named trigger fires. //Kūkali// waits, patient, remaining in suspense: the island parks rather than freezes, and it resumes EXACTLY ONCE — subscribeOnce semantics.

`trigger` names the `#slot` fragment of a papalohe wire in the same carrier. Omitted, the wait takes the first reaction that arrives. Papalohe declares the wire; kukali declares the wait at the receiving end.

''The trigger rides as a NAMED parameter,'' under either separator — `trigger="x"` and `trigger:x` both reach the slot, since a call binds a name through `=` and `:` alike.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/render>>

!! Render

''The page stays clear.'' A wait governs execution and never layout, so the procedure hands the compile layer a data annotation and renders nothing visible:

```
<span class="lar-kukali" data-kukali-trigger=<<trigger>> hidden="true"/>
```

The declaration rides in `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/sigil-kukali.tid` with `lar-kind: leaf`, its match pattern, and `lar-see-also: \suspends`. No template cascade stands here — an annotation carrying no layout needs no override seam.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

